WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:04.649
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute Papers
with Dr. Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:04.649 --> 00:00:11.879
Today we are going to do some incredible experiments
with NVIDIA’s next level image editor AI.

00:00:11.879 --> 00:00:18.550
Now, there are already many AI-based techniques
out there that are extremely good at creating

00:00:18.550 --> 00:00:23.029
new human, or even animal faces.

00:00:23.029 --> 00:00:30.570
You see here how beautifully this Alias-Free
GAN technique can morph one result into another.

00:00:30.570 --> 00:00:33.820
It truly is a sight to behold.

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:36.790
They are really good at editing images.

00:00:36.790 --> 00:00:41.190
You see, this was possible just a year ago.

00:00:41.190 --> 00:00:46.750
But, this new one, this can do more semantic
edits to our images.

00:00:46.750 --> 00:00:52.100
Let’s dive in and see the all the amazing
things that it can do!

00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:55.860
If we take a photo of our friends we haven’t
seen in a while.

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:56.860
What happens?

00:00:56.860 --> 00:01:03.470
Well of course, the eyes are closed, or are
barely open.

00:01:03.470 --> 00:01:06.160
From now on, this is not a problem.

00:01:06.160 --> 00:01:07.160
Done!

00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:14.630
And, if we wish to add a smile or take it
away, boom, that is also possible.

00:01:14.630 --> 00:01:19.820
Also, the universal classic, looking too much
into the camera?

00:01:19.820 --> 00:01:20.820
Not a problem.

00:01:20.820 --> 00:01:21.820
Done!

00:01:21.820 --> 00:01:29.930
Now, the AI can do even more kinds of edits,
hairstyle, eyebrows, wrinkles, you name it.

00:01:29.930 --> 00:01:32.790
However, that’s even not the best part.

00:01:32.790 --> 00:01:34.920
You have seen nothing yet!

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:37.100
Are you ready for the best part?

00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:40.390
Hold on to your papers, and check this out!

00:01:40.390 --> 00:01:44.720
Yes, it even works on drawings… paintings.

00:01:44.720 --> 00:01:46.820
Oh my!

00:01:46.820 --> 00:01:51.270
And even statues as well.

00:01:51.270 --> 00:01:52.270
Absolutely amazing.

00:01:52.270 --> 00:01:53.920
How cool is that?

00:01:53.920 --> 00:01:55.890
I love it.

00:01:55.890 --> 00:02:00.040
Researchers refer to these as out of domain
examples.

00:02:00.040 --> 00:02:03.870
The best part is that this is a proper learning-based
method.

00:02:03.870 --> 00:02:08.920
This means that by learning on human portraits,
it has obtained general knowledge.

00:02:08.920 --> 00:02:16.570
So now, it doesn’t just understand these
as clumps of pixels, it now understands concepts.

00:02:16.570 --> 00:02:22.970
Thus, it can reuse its knowledge, even when
facing a completely different kind of image,

00:02:22.970 --> 00:02:25.530
just like the ones you see here.

00:02:25.530 --> 00:02:31.420
This looks like science fiction, and here
it is, right in front of our eyes!

00:02:31.420 --> 00:02:32.420
Wow.

00:02:32.420 --> 00:02:34.840
But, it doesn’t stop there.

00:02:34.840 --> 00:02:38.870
It can also perform semantic image editing.

00:02:38.870 --> 00:02:40.210
What is that?

00:02:40.210 --> 00:02:41.910
Well, look!

00:02:41.910 --> 00:02:48.740
We can upload an image, look at the labels
of these images, and edit the labels themselves.

00:02:48.740 --> 00:02:53.210
Well, okay, but what is all that good for?

00:02:53.210 --> 00:02:59.100
Well, the AI understands how these labels
correspond to the real photo.

00:02:59.100 --> 00:03:08.290
So, check this out, we do the easy part, edit
the labels, and the AI does the hard part,

00:03:08.290 --> 00:03:10.730
changing the photo appropriately.

00:03:10.730 --> 00:03:12.240
Look!

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:13.760
Yes!

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:15.680
This is just incredible.

00:03:15.680 --> 00:03:22.240
The best part is that we are now even seeing
a hint of creativity with some of these solutions.

00:03:22.240 --> 00:03:28.130
And, if you are also one of those folks who
feel like the wheels and rims are never big

00:03:28.130 --> 00:03:32.780
enough, well, NVIDIA has got you covered,
that’s for sure.

00:03:32.780 --> 00:03:39.530
And here comes the kicker - it learned to
create these labels automatically by itself.

00:03:39.530 --> 00:03:45.730
So, how many label to image pairs did it have
to look at to perform all this?

00:03:45.730 --> 00:03:49.050
Well, what you do think?

00:03:49.050 --> 00:03:50.100
Millions?

00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:51.520
Hundreds of thousands.

00:03:51.520 --> 00:03:56.010
Please leave a comment, I’d love to hear
what you think.

00:03:56.010 --> 00:03:58.120
And the answer is 16.

00:03:58.120 --> 00:03:59.220
What?

00:03:59.220 --> 00:04:01.420
16 million?

00:04:01.420 --> 00:04:03.620
Nope. 16.

00:04:03.620 --> 00:04:06.310
Two to the power of four.

00:04:06.310 --> 00:04:07.690
That’s it.

00:04:07.690 --> 00:04:12.750
Well that is one of the most jaw-dropping
facts about this paper.

00:04:12.750 --> 00:04:17.280
This AI can learn general concepts from very
few examples.

00:04:17.280 --> 00:04:23.050
We don’t need to label the entirety of the
internet to have this technique be able to

00:04:23.050 --> 00:04:24.880
do its magic.

00:04:24.880 --> 00:04:27.680
That is absolutely incredible.

00:04:27.680 --> 00:04:31.120
Real learning from just 16 examples.

00:04:31.120 --> 00:04:32.230
Wow.

00:04:32.230 --> 00:04:37.780
The supplementary materials also showcase
loads of results, so, make sure to have a

00:04:37.780 --> 00:04:39.100
look at that.

00:04:39.100 --> 00:04:45.400
If you do, you’ll find that it can even
take an image of a bird, and adjust their

00:04:45.400 --> 00:04:49.620
beak sizes, even to extreme proportions.

00:04:49.620 --> 00:04:50.620
Very amusing.

00:04:50.620 --> 00:04:57.590
Or, we can even ask them to look up, and I
have to say, if no one would tell me that

00:04:57.590 --> 00:05:02.180
these are synthetic images, I might not be
able to tell.

00:05:02.180 --> 00:05:07.890
Now note that some of these capabilities were
present in previous techniques, but this new

00:05:07.890 --> 00:05:15.450
method does all of these with really high
quality, and all this in one elegant package.

00:05:15.450 --> 00:05:17.230
What a time to be alive!

00:05:17.230 --> 00:05:20.130
Now, of course, not even this technique is
perfect.

00:05:20.130 --> 00:05:26.360
There are still cases that are so far outside
of the training set of the AI that the result

00:05:26.360 --> 00:05:29.280
becomes completely unusable.

00:05:29.280 --> 00:05:34.090
And this is the perfect place to invoke the
first law of papers.

00:05:34.090 --> 00:05:35.300
What is that?

00:05:35.300 --> 00:05:40.010
Well, the First Law Of Papers says that research
is a process.

00:05:40.010 --> 00:05:45.760
Do not look at where we are, look at where
we will be two more papers down the line.

00:05:45.760 --> 00:05:53.680
And don’t forget, a couple papers before
this we were lucky to do this.

00:05:53.680 --> 00:05:56.740
And now, see how far we’ve come.

00:05:56.740 --> 00:06:00.130
This is incredible progress in just one year.

00:06:00.130 --> 00:06:02.790
So, what do you think?

00:06:02.790 --> 00:06:04.340
What would you use this for?

00:06:04.340 --> 00:07:07.150
I’d love to hear your thoughts, please let
me know in the comments below.

00:07:07.150 --> 00:07:11.120
Thanks for watching and for your generous
support, and I'll see you next time!

